{"race":{"race_url":"https://www.naturetime.es/en/ultra-trail-serra-montsant-4/","town":"Ulldemolins","race_name":"UTSM Serra de Montsant"},"fetched_at":"2026-08-26T16:04:58.810Z","pages":[{"url":"https://www.naturetime.es/en/ultra-trail-serra-montsant-4/","hash":"02fe8356be6165131007b993b0601295c154bb1334256934ae5a1df16e5ef00b","chars":12000,"text":"Español Català English Select Page OTSO ULTRA Trail SERRA MONTSANT-COSTA DAURADA 17TH EDITION 10th & 11th october 2026 >>3.000€ in prizes<< Open for registration UTSM 2026 STARTS IN ... Day(s) : Hour(s) : Minute(s) : Second(s)  PRESENTATION  TECHNICAL DATA  ROUTES  REGISTRTATIONS  PROGRAMME  RUNNER'S BAG  +info  PHOTOS/SN  VOLUNTEERS  SPONSORS PRESENTATION OTSO ULTRA Trail SERRA DE MONTSANT-COSTA DAURADA / 17TH EDITION OCTOBER, 10TH-11TH The OTSO UTSM COSTA DAURADA was born from the idea of ​​creating a balanced encounter between a natural environment of a very special value, such as that of the Serra de Montsant Natural Park; the people who inhabit the villages integrated in the territory and the athletes who, with their strong sports and human commitment, will be the ones who will trace the route that unites them 2026 utsm PRESENTATION (read more) The competition reaches its seventeenth edition, after its debut in 2009 and the year-on-year increase in participants. OTSO UTSM COSTA DAURADA is an accessible footrace, despite its 63km and 3,470m of elevation gain, designed to offer the experience of running in total freedom and semi-autonomy within a setting steeped in eremitic tradition, once a haven for ascetics and anchorites. The perfect environment is Monte Santo (hence its name, Montsant). Besides the main event, the ULTRA 63k distance, there are five other races, all very interesting: MSM 44km: awarded 2 ITRA points and a qualifier for the UTMB 50k. This year it is part of the FEEC Endurance Cup. The short trails on Sunday, October 11: 25km-11km-7km. The last two have versions for walkers. And in this edition, we re bringing back the MONTSANT STAGE RUN 88k stage race: Saturday 63km and Sunday 25km. ITRA POINTS: The UTSM is a UTMB qualifying race. The main event (63km) awards 3 points in the ranking, and we re keeping the TSM25k with 1 point in the new ranking. The Marathon-MSM will provide 2 ITRA points and will qualify for the UTMB 50k. The stage race is rated as 4 ITRA points and 100K UTMB Index. NOTE: The event takes place over two days: Saturday, October 10th: 88k stage run + 63k ultra + 44k marathon / Sunday, October 11th: TSM25k + TSM12k + trek12 + 7k start trail. NEW FOR 2026: We maintain the Environmental Quality Seal at Petjada Verda FEEC! technical data 88KM - MONTSANT STAGE RUN (63KM + 25KM) MONTSANT STAGE RUN STAGE RUN MODALITY (2 DAYS) 4 ITRA points 100K UTMB Distance: Stage 1 SATURDAY 10TH OCTOBER : 63Km + Stage 2 SUNDAY 11TH OCTOBER : 25km. Total: 88km Positive slope: Stage 1: 3.470m (Saturday October 10th)+ Stage 2: 1.263m (Sunday October 11th).Total: 4.733m D+ Maximum time: Stage 1: 15h + Stage 2: 6h * IMPORTANT NOTE : Between the two stages you will not be able to rest in the finish area, since it will be closed once the last runner of the 63km distance finishes. Runners must regain strength in their chosen accommodation option. CATEGORIES Masculine Femenine PRIZES To the 1st, 2nd and 3rd of the general masculine and femenine classification Prizes are NOT accumulative ULTRA TRAIL SERRA DE MONTSANT 63km Saturday October 10th 2026 3 ITRA points 100K UTMB Distance: 64,3Km Positive slope: 3.470m Maximum time: 15h 1st Starting time: 8:00h Starting place: Swimming pool, in Ulldemolins center town REFRESHMENT POSTS*: Km 8,7 AVI 0: WATER (Tres Juradets-St. Bartomeu) Km 23,0 AVI 0: Margalef dam Km 27,3 AVI 2: Fonda Margalef outsite Km 31,6 AGUA: Mountain natural fontain Sant Salvador Ermitage km 40,4 AVI 2: La Morera de Montsant Km 52,0 AVI 1: Albarca (Roig Hill Outsite) Km 60,1 AVI 0: Santa Magdalena Ermitage outsite Km 62,76 AVI 2: Ulldemolins FINISH LINE. TYPES OF REFRESHMENTS AVI 0: water, soft drinks, fruit, energetic bar,. AVI 1: water, soft drinks, cheese/ham small sandwiches, fruit, biscuits, nuts, isotonic drinks, etc. AVI 2: AVI1 + pasta ISOTONIC Will allow us to find Isotonic drinks to consume on-site at the following points : Margalef Dam Margalef Morera de Montsant Albarca * We advise you to review the TIMMING technical document where exactly the type of provisioning and mileage point is specified according to the modality. ECO-RACE There will be not plastic glasses throughout the race. You must to have a reusable glass on the race. If you want. the organization will sell you a special glass to be used throughout the race. Liquid provisioning posta will only have water. At the light and complete provisioning posts there will be other drinks, but they can only be drunk in situ. Cans or other racers’ drink containers can only be filled with water. External assistance It is forbidden to receive external aid or to be accompanied by other people that are not racers registered in the race. External assistance is ONLY permitted in the LIGHT and COMPLETE provisioning posts areas only for 1 person (Margalef + La Morera de Montsant + Albarca + Santa Magdalena Ermitage). Outside these areas, external help or assistance is forbidden. Racers are responsible for their own food or hydration during the race. It is advisable a minimum of calories at the beginning of the race ensure a semi-autonomous participation in the race. At the finishing line, there will be an AV2 provisioning post. CATEGORIES Sub23 masculine (21 – 23 years old) Sub23 femenine (21 – 23 years old) Veteran masculine (40 – 49 years old) Veteran femenine (40 – 49 years old) Master maculine (50- 59 years old) Master femenine (50 – 59 years old) Master plus masculine (60 or older) Master plus femenine (60 or older) PRIZES 1st, 2nd, 3rd racer of the Masculine and Feminine General Classification. Economic prizes. 1st racer of each category. Non economic pri